            "title": "China talks are complicated - POLITICO",
            "snippets": [
              "# China talks are complicated\n**— U.S. officials are cautious about being too hopeful about China trade talks,** with U.S. Trade Representative Robert Lighthizer making clear to lawmakers earlier this month that the deadline for tariff escalation would not be extended.\n\n**— U.S. officials are denying Huawei’s legal troubles will sour trade talks with China**, but the administration will likely send its formal extradition request for a Huawei executive detained in Canada the same day the negotiations begin",
              "**CHINA TALKS ARE COMPLICATED:** Lighthizer provided little hope to House lawmakers that the administration would stave off the escalation of tariffs against China by extending a March 1 deadline for reaching a trade deal over Beijing’s trade practices",
              "In a Jan. 17 meeting with Ways and Means members, the top trade official told lawmakers the Trump administration has no plans at this point to provide any additional time for the two sides to reach a deal if they fail to meet that deadline, three House aides told Morning Trade. The firm date raises the stakes for the two sides to reach some sort of agreement in the next four weeks before tariffs on hundreds of billions of dollars worth of Chinese imports are set to more than double, from 10 percent to 25 percent, on March 2",
              "**Mnuchin: There’s still time:** Treasury Secretary Steven Mnuchin downplayed the potential of sealing a deal with Chinese officials when they come to town Jan. 30-31, but said there is still time to reach agreement. Chinese Vice Premier Liu He, who is leading the talks for Beijing, is expected to meet with President Donald Trump during his visit, Mnuchin said",
              "“Let me just remind people, we do have another 30 days after this so my expectation is we’ll make significant progress at these meetings, but I would just emphasize these are complicated issues,” Mnuchin said Monday at a White House press briefing. “We have a timeline that we’ve mapped out the 90 days.”",
              "White House chief economic adviser Larry Kudlow said he didn’t want to make any predictions on whether the meeting will produce a framework for an agreement. He said Trump has expressed some “guarded optimism” about the talks but noted that they are “very difficult; very, very important.”\n\n**Enforcement is the name of the game:** Both Mnuchin and Kudlow stressed the importance of a final deal that holds China to any commitments it makes when it comes to protecting U.S. technology and intellectual property",
